From 1fa7e5554c5f0a4941487b77c474f82623b16fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:28:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat(documenteditor): Word-like title bar with command
 search
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- File name (without extension, like Word) followed by the save state:
  Saved, Saving… (spinning), Not saved when autosave is off, Offline;
  it follows the editor save actions and the Save button state.
- Clicking the name opens a flyout: rename the file in place when the
  host supports it (same rename event as before), its location, Open
  file location and Version history.
- Centred "Search (Alt+Q)" box, Alt+Q (Ctrl+Option+Q on macOS) focuses
  it like in Word. It searches the ribbon commands - every button of
  the ribbon tabs and the items of their menus, with their tab and group
  - and runs the chosen one by switching to its tab and clicking it, so
  "table" opens the Insert > Table grid. Suggested actions when empty;
  Find and Replace in the document as the last entries. Arrow keys,
  Enter and Esc work as in Word.
- Tab row: Comments button (toggles the comments pane), the Editing /
  Reviewing / Viewing mode drop-down and an accent Share button (host
  sharing, or the Share page of the File menu); the magnifier and the
  open-location buttons give way to the search box and the flyout.

Alt+Q opened the chat panel before; the chat stays in the Review tab.
Strings in en and the 11 UI languages.

[branding]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
